L0103: Chained comparison

Comparisons are binary expressions. A spelling such as a < b < c does not implicitly mean two comparisons joined by conjunction. Write a < b && b < c inside the appropriate runtime or proposition context.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/chained_comparison.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// Comparisons chained without parentheses: an error, as in Rust.
fn between(a: u8, b: u8, c: u8) -> bool {
    a < b < c
}

fn same(a: u8, b: u8, c: bool) -> bool {
    a == b == c
}
```

Language, as built: [1.6:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.6:1).
